"Seconde","2nde"],"voiceOnly":false},{"id":"1re","stage":"lycee","year":11,"age":16,"name":{"en":"1re","local":{"fr":"Première"}},"aliases":["Première","1ère"],"voiceOnly":false},{"id":"terminale","stage":"lycee","year":12,"age":17,"name":{"en":"Terminale","local":{"fr":"Terminale"}},"aliases":["Tle","Term"],"voiceOnly":false}],"until":null,"notes":"The State sets programmes and the vice-rectorat runs secondary schooling: six collèges (6e–3e), the Lycée d'État (general and technological) and an agricultural lycée. Primary (10 écoles) was conceded in 1969 to the Catholic mission's Direction de l'enseignement catholique; a 2025 law moved its teachers to the State. The school year starts in February, and many children born in the second half of the year start a year late. Maternelle is left out, so CP (age 6) is year 1. The brevet closes 3e and the baccalauréat Terminale."}]
